<!--/Post: 11953-->
<!--Post: 11975--><!--Time: 1111470627-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11975"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Z, <BR> <BR>I normally would agree that it would be excessive except that E&#39;s information and insight seems to be a driving force. E&#39;s the straw that stirs the drink. It looks as if E is putting lots of energy into research and sharing information. It seems this mostly valuable information comes from sources possibly close to the case ?????? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
